IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), s 201(16) to (23) (Part 6, Division 1): the directors' statement that accompanies the financial statements
-- (what it must contain is the Twelfth Schedule, sgc1-sch12.l4), representations about reserves, banking corporations, charities, and the savings
-- for financial years ending before 1 July 2015. (1) to (11) are in sgc1-s201.l4, (12) to (15A) in sgc1-s201-departures.l4.
-- The transitional subsections (20) to (23) are encoded, though they affect few now: "inert" is allowed only where no one is affected, and a
-- late return for an old financial year still can be (NOTES.md, fork register).

§ `Section 201(16) to (23): the acts of the regulative rules`

DECLARE `s 201(16) to (23) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 201(16) accompany the financial statements with the directors' statement`
    `s 201(17) publish a document or advertisement that represents that the company has a reserve without the accompanying statement`
    `s 201(23) attach a copy of the report prepared under section 201(5) as in force before 1 July 2015 to the return`

§ `Section 201(16): the directors' statement`

-- src:18129 | (16) The financial statements laid before a company at its general
-- src:18130 | meeting (including any consolidated financial statements annexed to
-- src:18131 | the balance sheet of a parent company) must be accompanied, before
-- src:18132 | the auditor reports on the financial statements under this Part, by a
-- src:18133 | statement signed on behalf of the directors by 2 directors of the
-- src:18134 | company containing the information set out in the Twelfth Schedule.
@ref s 201(16) (src:18129-18134)
GIVEN `the financial statements laid before the company at its general meeting are accompanied by a statement of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors who have signed the statement on behalf of the directors` IS A NUMBER
      `the statement contains the information set out in the Twelfth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement accompanied the financial statements before the auditor reported on them under Part 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(16) the financial statements are accompanied by the directors' statement the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the financial statements laid before the company at its general meeting are accompanied by a statement of the directors`
       AND `the number of directors who have signed the statement on behalf of the directors` AT LEAST 2
       AND `the statement contains the information set out in the Twelfth Schedule`
       AND `the statement accompanied the financial statements before the auditor reported on them under Part 6`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The financial statements laid before a company at its general meeting ... must be accompanied, before the auditor reports on the financial statements under this Part, by a statement signed on behalf of the directors by 2 directors of the company containing the information set out in the Twelfth Schedule" (a duty not met: the provision's own question; "2 directors" read as at least 2: fork line F-16 of NOTES.md)

-- The time the text gives is "before the auditor reports": the clock counts days from the start of the trace.
@ref s 201(16) (src:18129-18134)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from now until the auditor reports on the financial statements` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201(16) to (23) act`
`s 201(16) the directors must accompany the financial statements with a statement signed on their behalf by 2 directors` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 201(16) accompany the financial statements with the directors' statement`
    WITHIN `the number of days from now until the auditor reports on the financial statements`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the financial statements were not accompanied by the directors' statement before the auditor reported on them"

§ `Section 201(17): representations that the company has a reserve`

-- src:18138 | (17) Any document (other than any financial statements or a
-- src:18139 | balance sheet prepared in accordance with this Act) or advertisement
-- src:18140 | published, issued or circulated by or on behalf of a company (other
-- src:18141 | than a banking corporation) must not contain any direct or indirect
-- src:18142 | representation that the company has any reserve unless the
-- src:18143 | representation is accompanied —
-- src:18145 | (a) if the reserve is invested outside the business of the
-- src:18146 | company — by a statement showing the manner in which
-- src:18147 | and the security upon which it is invested; or
-- src:18152 | (b) if the reserve is being used in the business of the
-- src:18153 | company — by a statement to the effect that the reserve
-- src:18154 | is being so used.
@ref s 201(17) (src:18138-18154)
GIVEN `the document or advertisement is a financial statement or a balance sheet prepared in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a banking corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or advertisement contains a direct or indirect representation that the company has a reserve` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reserve is invested outside the business of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representation is accompanied by a statement showing the manner in which and the security upon which the reserve is invested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reserve is being used in the business of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representation is accompanied by a statement to the effect that the reserve is being so used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(17) the representation that the company has a reserve is barred` MEANS
    IF `the document or advertisement is a financial statement or a balance sheet prepared in accordance with this Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any document (other than any financial statements or a balance sheet prepared in accordance with this Act) or advertisement ... must not contain any direct or indirect representation that the company has any reserve" (the parenthesis takes financial statements out of the bar)
    ELSE IF `the company is a banking corporation`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "published, issued or circulated by or on behalf of a company (other than a banking corporation)" (the parenthesis takes a banking corporation out of the bar)
         ELSE IF NOT `the document or advertisement contains a direct or indirect representation that the company has a reserve`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not contain any direct or indirect representation that the company has any reserve" (a document with no such representation is not barred: the bar's own question)
              ELSE IF    (`the reserve is invested outside the business of the company` AND `the representation is accompanied by a statement showing the manner in which and the security upon which the reserve is invested`)
                      OR (`the reserve is being used in the business of the company` AND `the representation is accompanied by a statement to the effect that the reserve is being so used`)
                   THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the representation is accompanied — (a) if the reserve is invested outside the business of the company — by a statement showing the manner in which and the security upon which it is invested; or (b) if the reserve is being used in the business of the company — by a statement to the effect that the reserve is being so used" (the "unless" is met)
                   ELSE IF `the reserve is invested outside the business of the company` OR `the reserve is being used in the business of the company`
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraphs (a) and (b) name a reserve invested outside the business and a reserve used in the business, and the subsection is silent on a reserve that is neither

-- A prohibition: the act is the forbidden publication. No time limit; a trace with no events reads as a standing obligation.
@ref s 201(17) (src:18138-18154)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201(16) to (23) act`
`s 201(17) a company must not publish a document that represents that it has a reserve unless the representation is accompanied` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 201(17) publish a document or advertisement that represents that the company has a reserve without the accompanying statement`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company published a document or advertisement representing that it has a reserve without the statement section 201(17) requires"

§ `Section 201(18): banking corporations`

-- src:18158 | (18) The provisions of this Act relating to the form and content of
-- src:18159 | the statement of directors and the annual financial statements apply to
-- src:18160 | a banking corporation with such modifications and exceptions as are
-- src:18161 | determined either generally or in any particular case by the Monetary
-- src:18162 | Authority of Singapore established under section 3 of the Monetary
-- src:18163 | Authority of Singapore Act 1970.
@ref s 201(18) (src:18158-18163)
GIVEN `the company is a banking corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Monetary Authority of Singapore has determined modifications or exceptions, generally or in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(18) the form and content provisions apply to the banking corporation as they stand` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a banking corporation`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a banking corporation" and says nothing of any other company
    ELSE IF `the Monetary Authority of Singapore has determined modifications or exceptions, generally or in the particular case`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "with such modifications and exceptions as are determined either generally or in any particular case by the Monetary Authority of Singapore": the determination is not among the sources
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 201(19): charities and institutions of a public character`

-- src:18167 | (19) In respect of a company that is registered as a charity or
-- src:18168 | approved as an institution of a public character under the Charities
-- src:18169 | Act 1994, the requirements of this section as to the form and content
-- src:18170 | of a company’s financial statements or consolidated financial
-- src:18171 | statements being in compliance with the Accounting Standards
-- src:18172 | apply subject to any modification prescribed under section 12(1)(f) of
-- src:18173 | that Act in respect of such a company.
@ref s 201(19) (src:18167-18173)
GIVEN `the company is registered as a charity or approved as an institution of a public character under the Charities Act 1994` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a modification has been prescribed under section 12(1)(f) of the Charities Act 1994 in respect of such a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(19) the Accounting Standards requirements apply to the charity as they stand` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is registered as a charity or approved as an institution of a public character under the Charities Act 1994`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a company that is registered as a charity or approved as an institution of a public character" and says nothing of any other company
    ELSE IF `a modification has been prescribed under section 12(1)(f) of the Charities Act 1994 in respect of such a company`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any modification prescribed under section 12(1)(f) of that Act": the modification is not among the sources
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 201(20) and (21): references to the financial statements before 1 July 2015`

-- src:18177 | (20) For the purposes of subsections (1) and (5), a reference to the
-- src:18178 | preceding financial statements includes the profit and loss account,
-- src:18179 | balance sheet and consolidated accounts required to be laid before the
-- src:18180 | company at its annual general meeting under section 201 in force
-- src:18181 | before 1 July 2015.
@ref s 201(20) (src:18177-18181)
GIVEN `the documents are the profit and loss account, balance sheet and consolidated accounts required to be laid before the company at its annual general meeting under section 201 as in force before 1 July 2015` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(20) the documents are within a reference to the preceding financial statements` MEANS
    IF `the documents are the profit and loss account, balance sheet and consolidated accounts required to be laid before the company at its annual general meeting under section 201 as in force before 1 July 2015`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference to the preceding financial statements includes ..." leaves the list open

-- src:18185 | (21) For the purposes of subsections (1) and (5), a reference to the
-- src:18186 | requirement to lay financial statements before a company includes
-- src:18187 | the laying of the profit and loss account, balance sheet and
-- src:18188 | consolidated accounts prepared in accordance with section 201 in
-- src:18189 | force immediately before 1 July 2015, where such profit and loss
-- src:18190 | account, balance sheet and consolidated accounts have been prepared
-- src:18191 | in respect of a financial year which ended before 1 July 2015.
@ref s 201(21) (src:18185-18191)
GIVEN `the profit and loss account, balance sheet and consolidated accounts were prepared in accordance with section 201 as in force immediately before 1 July 2015` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial year in respect of which they were prepared ended on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(21) the laying of the documents is within a reference to the requirement to lay financial statements` MEANS
    IF    `the profit and loss account, balance sheet and consolidated accounts were prepared in accordance with section 201 as in force immediately before 1 July 2015`
       AND `the financial year in respect of which they were prepared ended on` LESS THAN Date 1 7 2015
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference to the requirement to lay financial statements before a company includes ..." leaves the list open

§ `Section 201(22) and (23): financial years that ended before 1 July 2015`

-- src:18195 | (22) Subsection (16) does not apply to any company in respect of
-- src:18196 | any financial year which ended before 1 July 2015; and
-- src:18197 | section 201(5) to (8), (11), (12) and (15) in force immediately
-- src:18202 | before that date continues to apply to such company for that financial
-- src:18203 | year.
@ref s 201(22) (src:18195-18203)
GIVEN `the financial year ended on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(22) subsection (16) applies to the company for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `the financial year ended on` LESS THAN Date 1 7 2015
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (16) does not apply to any company in respect of any financial year which ended before 1 July 2015" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only that (16) does not apply to a financial year that ended before 1 July 2015; for a later one it says nothing and subsection (16) applies by its own terms

@ref s 201(22) (src:18195-18203)
GIVEN `the financial year ended on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(22) the earlier provisions of section 201 continue to apply to the company for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `the financial year ended on` LESS THAN Date 1 7 2015
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "section 201(5) to (8), (11), (12) and (15) in force immediately before that date continues to apply to such company for that financial year" speaks of a financial year that ended before 1 July 2015 and is silent on a later one

-- src:18207 | (23) Without limiting section 197(2), a company referred to in
-- src:18208 | subsection (22) must, when lodging a return with the Registrar under
-- src:18209 | section 197, attach a copy of the report prepared in accordance with
-- src:18210 | section 201(5) in force immediately before 1 July 2015.
@ref s 201(23) (src:18207-18210)
GIVEN `the financial year ended on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(23) the company must attach a copy of the report prepared under section 201(5) as it then stood to the return` MEANS
    IF `the financial year ended on` LESS THAN Date 1 7 2015
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a company referred to in subsection (22)", a company with a financial year that ended before 1 July 2015, and is silent on any other

-- No time limit and no consequence inside the subsection ("when lodging a return"): no trace can show a breach (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 201(23) (src:18207-18210)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201(16) to (23) act`
`s 201(23) a company with an old financial year must attach a copy of the report to its return` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 201(23) attach a copy of the report prepared under section 201(5) as in force before 1 July 2015 to the return`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 201(23) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not attach a copy of the report prepared under section 201(5) as in force before 1 July 2015 to the return" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
